  "headline": "Cadence is projected default-alive on its current growth trajectory, but the model is too thin to support a fundraise without significant structural expansion.",
  "investor_talking_points": [
    "At 8% monthly growth and 75% gross margins, we're projected to reach cash-flow breakeven without raising — which means any round we do raise is for acceleration, not survival.",
    "Our static runway is 12.5 months at current burn, giving us time to fundraise from a position of strength rather than urgency.",
    "Gross margin of 75% is at the top of the seed-stage SaaS benchmark range, validating the unit economics foundation."
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "runway": {
      "callout": "The model projects Cadence reaches cash-flow breakeven around month 19 (roughly early 2028 from June 2026) and never depletes cash — a default-alive result.",
